// CROWN — string interpolation allocates (it lowers to concatenation), so
// a body declared `!Alloc` that interpolates is refused.
// Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean through the pinned boot (measured 2026-09-23): the
// interpolation charges nothing while `++` charges Alloc.
fn mk(x) with !Alloc = "a{x}b"
fn main() = 0
